    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0461" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg441"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 2d of June last, No. 77, and accompanying correspondence,
                    respecting the case of James White. With regard to the pressing need of
                    increased assistance in the different branches of our service in China, so
                    reasonably solicited and supported by yourself and by Mr. Seward, I shall not
                    fail to make a representation to Congress on the subject, at its ensuing
                    session.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
